## t1 - An expected value never comes from the code under test

All assertions use literal expected values: string literals (`"gap"`), numeric literals (`3`, `0`), or boolean relations (`!attrs.contains_key()`, `!key.starts_with()`). The code under test is exercised to produce the actual values being compared, but every expectation is written as a literal or a relation defined in the test itself, not derived from running the code.

